Introduction:
Step 1: Install Vite
npm install -g vite

This will install Vite globally, allowing you to use it across multiple projects.
Step 2: Create a New Project
vite new my-project

This will create a new directory called my-project containing the basic files and folders needed to get started with Vite.
Step 3: Configure Vite
vite.config.js file in the root of your project and add the following code:
module.exports = {
  // Enable TypeScript support
  typescript: true,

  // Set the entry point for the application
  entry: './src/index.tsx',

  // Define the output configuration
  output: {
    path: 'build',
    filename: 'index.js',
    publicPath: '/'
  },

  // Add plugin for TypeScript support
  plugins: [
    new VitePlugin({
      tsConfig: 'tsconfig.json'
    })
  ]
};

